==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyUniqueEvents  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyUniqueEvents.als
    rationale: Clearing the unique-event constraint lets Alloy construct two distinct AuditEntries that describe the same logical event (same recording operation, same auditOp, same affectedSharee) — the structural signature of an audit log that has been mutated/duplicated, which is exactly what AppendOnly rejects.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionEnforced  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_PermissionEnforced.als
    rationale: Removing the permission-enforcement fact lets the model invent a successful operation whose (relationship, kind) is not in the permission matrix — the canonical least-privilege violation (e.g., an in-team non-related member who successfully GETs a task).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalent404  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ByteEquivalent404.als
    rationale: Clearing the 404-response rule frees a cross-team caller to receive a non-404 response, revealing existence of a task in another tenant — the multi-tenant information-leakage failure FR-014 is designed to block.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_ByteEquivalent404
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalent404: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditPerSuccessfulMutation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditPerSuccessfulMutation.als
    rationale: Removing the audit-per-mutation linkage lets a successful PATCH/DELETE exist with no AuditEntry — a direct violation of SC-007's 'no observable state change without an audit entry' invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerMutation
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredEverywhere  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuthRequiredEverywhere.als
    rationale: Clearing the auth gate lets an unauthenticated request flag itself as successful, which is the canonical FR-001 failure (handler runs before token introspection).
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing the attribution fact lets the actor recorded on an AuditEntry diverge from the caller of the recording Operation — misattribution, which FR-016 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditFieldsConsistent
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditFieldsConsistent: FAIL (expected)

